    "perplexity": {
      "description": "The Genius After Hours is a 1961 Atlantic album that presents Ray Charles in an all-instrumental, jazz-oriented setting, highlighting his piano as the lead voice rather than his famous singing. Recorded from sessions in 1956 and 1957, it draws on the same era as The Great Ray Charles and shows him working comfortably in hard bop, blues, and R&B-inflected jazz.\n\nThe album is often valued as a quieter, more intimate companion to his more celebrated soul and gospel recordings, with a relaxed late-night feel that suits the title. Its mix of standards and originals shows Charles’ command of melody, swing, and groove, and it has long been appreciated by listeners who want to hear his musicianship away from his vocal persona.",
